# Shared version stamp for the two drawing sets:
#     as3935-node-wiring.pdf        (make-wiring-diagram.py)
#     as3935-protoboard-layout.pdf  (make-protoboard-layout.py)
#
# Both generators read the first non-comment line below and print it, centred,
# in every page footer. The two documents are only usable together -- the wire
# references in one are the hole coordinates in the other -- so a printout of
# each should carry the same stamp. If they do not, one of them is stale.
#
# THIS IS A DATE, NOT A REVISION NUMBER, and deliberately so: every page also
# carries "revision 2", which is the HARDWARE revision (README 16). A "v1" here
# next to a "revision 2" there reads as a contradiction, and did. A date cannot
# be mistaken for either.
#
# Format: YYYY-MM-DD, with a lowercase letter appended if the drawings change
# more than once in a day (2026-09-09, then 2026-09-09b, 2026-09-09c ...).
#
# Bump it whenever EITHER drawing changes, then regenerate BOTH:
#     python3 make-wiring-diagram.py && python3 make-protoboard-layout.py
#
# Set by hand, not from today's date and not from git, so that re-running a
# generator without changing anything cannot produce a spurious new stamp.

2026-09-11b
